# Per-extension CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md files generated by `swamp repo init`
# The root CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md is the single source of project guidance
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md

# Root .claude/ directory (this repo's own Claude Code config) is not part
# of any individual extension, and stays untracked. Do the same for .agents
# from Opencode et al.
/.claude/
/.agents/

# Auto-installed swamp CLI skill bundles are regenerated by `swamp repo
# init`/`upgrade` in every extension subdirectory — not authored content, so
# not tracked there either. Everything else under an extension's .claude/
# (including any custom-authored skills) IS tracked; each extension's own
# generated .gitignore already excludes its noisy local-only files
# (worktrees/, settings.local.json, scheduled_tasks.*).
**/.claude/skills/swamp/
**/.claude/skills/swamp-getting-started/

# Git worktrees for isolated development
.worktrees/

# Swamp runtime state (databases, telemetry, caches, outputs)
# .swamp.yaml repo markers are NOT ignored — only the .swamp/ directory
**/.swamp/

# Session scratch files
next-prompt.md
**/TODO.md

# Tmp until i get them working better
.github/
scripts/
